ns from the basic ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSTheme","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and should be seen as the default theme for the OUDS library with the Orange brand colors for example.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"Theme Orange"},"doc://OUDSTokensSemantic/documentation/OUDSTokensSemantic/SizeSemanticToken":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SizeSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SizeSemanticToken","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/documentation\/OUDSTokensSemantic\/SizeSemanticToken","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/oudstokenssemantic\/sizesemantictoken","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Basically a size semantic token, used for width and height values, is a _ raw token,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it has the same final type, to keep grammar clean and clear with design system grammar."}],"role":"symbol","title":"SizeSemanticToken"}}}